Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: a queued swap is not completed before it is sent

tcpm_dr_set(), tcpm_pr_set() and tcpm_vconn_set() put their swap in
upcoming_state, start the AMS and wait for the swap to be completed.  A
message of the partner's that is handled before AMS_START has run and
that makes the port change state (new Source_Capabilities, a swap of the
partner's own) leaves the swap in upcoming_state.  The ready state that
follows completes the pending swap with status 0 first and only then
moves on to upcoming_state, where the swap is sent.

The writer has its answer before the swap is on the wire.  With the role
check in tcpm_dr_set() that answer is -EAGAIN, for a swap the partner
accepts a moment later.

Have the two ready states leave a pending swap alone while a state is
queued.  The swap is then completed by the states it goes through (a
refusal, the timeout) or by the ready state after them.  If the queued
state is another one, which has taken the swap's place, the ready state
after that one completes the swap as before and the role check says what
became of it.

When the message that got in first is the partner's DR_Swap, the port
accepts it and then sends the queued DR_Swap as well, which puts the
data role back: a write of "host" changes nothing, and a port with
tcpc->request_dfp_as_sink that asked for the host role ends up as
device with the matter settled.  Drop a queued DR_SWAP_SEND where the
partner's swap changes the role.  The role it was queued for is the one
the port gets there.

Neither has been seen on a tablet; both are read from the code.  The
window is the time between tcpm_ams_start() and AMS_START: tSinkTx for a
PD 3.x source, and for a sink a message that was received already and
waits for the port lock.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -5231,6 +5231,22 @@ static void tcpm_swap_complete(struct tc
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A ready state completes the swap that a write to one of the port's roles
+ * waits for.  Not while that swap still sits in upcoming_state, behind a
+ * message of the partner's that got in first: it has not been sent yet.  The
+ * states it goes through complete it, or the ready state after them.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_complete_ready(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	if (port->swap_pending && port->upcoming_state != INVALID_STATE) {
+		tcpm_log(port, "Swap is still queued, left pending");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	tcpm_swap_complete(port, 0);
+}
+
 static enum typec_pwr_opmode tcpm_get_pwr_opmode(enum typec_cc_status cc)
 {
 	switch (cc) {
@@ -5546,7 +5562,7 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 #endif
 		port->try_src_count = 0;
 
-		tcpm_swap_complete(port, 0);
+		tcpm_swap_complete_ready(port);
 		tcpm_typec_connect(port);
 
 		if (port->ams != NONE_AMS)
@@ -5935,7 +5951,7 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 
 		if (!port->pd_capable && port->slow_charger_loop)
 			tcpm_set_current_limit(port, tcpm_get_current_limit(port), 5000);
-		tcpm_swap_complete(port, 0);
+		tcpm_swap_complete_ready(port);
 		tcpm_typec_connect(port);
 		if (port->pd_capable && port->source_caps[0] & PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE)
 			mod_enable_frs_delayed_work(port, 0);
@@ -6233,6 +6249,14 @@ static void run_state_machine(struct tcp
 		/* Whoever asked for it, a completed swap settles the data role */
 		port->sink_dfp_done = true;
 		port->data_role_swapped = true;
+		/*
+		 * A swap of the port's own that was still queued when the
+		 * partner's came in asked for the role this one gives it.
+		 */
+		if (port->upcoming_state == DR_SWAP_SEND) {
+			tcpm_log(port, "Partner swapped first, queued DR_SWAP_SEND dropped");
+			port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+		}
 		tcpm_unregister_altmodes(port);
 		if (port->data_role == TYPEC_HOST)
 			tcpm_set_roles(port, true, TYPEC_STATE_USB, port->pwr_role,
